Ever play the game of mastermind?  That's what the drawbridge is like.  
Get yourself a bugle (magical or otherwise) and when it says "improvise?" 
say no and play the mastermind game.  I'll give a quickie 3 letter 
mastermind game.  Remember---the bugle plays musical notes.  So this 
means from A-G.  We'll do this methodically:

AAA

One click.

(this means that one is in the right place)

ABB

One tumbler.

(this means that the A note is either 2nd or 3rd position)

AAB

One click.

(this means that the A is in the second position)

CAC

Two clicks.

(This means that there is the A in the second position, and the C in 
either the 1st or 3rd positions)

CAA

Two clicks.

(That means that the first letter is C, the second is A)

CAD

The drawbridge comes down and kills you in the porticullis.

You die.

(This shows you that the combination was CAD.  Also---don't be under the 
drawbrdige when you open it---it can kill you.  If you're clever, do what 
I do...

You see a spoiled fortune cookie.  Eat it?  [ynq]


...open the drawbridge, let a monster cross onto it, and close it on them,
killing them instantly.)

OK: hope this helped.

